# Spyline: the phone controller and the game's pace.
# Save this file and phones pick up the change. Syntax and every setting: web/src/games/kit/pad.ts
# The phone shows the board. Agents tap a card to pick it; the handler's board shows the key, and on their turn a
# text field, a number and a Send button. The buttons below are drawn by controller.ts; they are listed here for the
# help sheet and their haptics.

controller
  orientation  portrait

button pick
  label        "Tap a card"
  hint         "Agents: tap a card to pick it, tap it again to take it back. When most of your team picks the same card, it is revealed."
  haptic       12ms

button stop
  label        "Stop guessing"
  hint         "Agents: end your team's turn (most of the team has to agree). After at least one card."
  haptic       16ms

button send
  label        "Send clue"
  hint         "Handlers: type one word and pick a number (how many of your cards it points to), then send it."
  haptic       20ms

buzz                         # ms on, off, on…
  turn         40 60 40      # your clue
  clue         30            # your handler gave a clue
  good         25
  bad          120
  burn         200 80 200
  win          40 40 40 40 120
  lose         300

tune                         # the computer players' pace, in ms
  bot-think    2600          # a handler bot thinks this long (plus up to half again)
  bot-look     1000          # an agent bot looks this long (plus up to the same again)
